<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">skills</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">skills</ansi> command lists your current known skills.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">skills</ansi>

<ansi fg="yellow">Combat Skills:</ansi>
  <ansi fg="stat">weapon-combat</ansi>  — Melee attack & defense with weapons
  <ansi fg="stat">unarmed-combat</ansi> — Fist/body attacks, grappling
  <ansi fg="stat">ranged-combat</ansi>  — Bows, crossbows, thrown weapons
  <ansi fg="stat">spellcasting</ansi>   — All magic offense & defense
  <ansi fg="stat">rhetoric</ansi>       — Conviction attacks (taunt)

<ansi fg="yellow">Utility Skills:</ansi>
  <ansi fg="stat">first-aid</ansi>     — Healing, treating wounds
  <ansi fg="stat">skullduggery</ansi>  — Sneaking, stealing, lockpicking
  <ansi fg="stat">search</ansi>        — Finding hidden things, tracking, foraging
  <ansi fg="stat">bartering</ansi>     — Trade prices, negotiation

<ansi fg="yellow">Crafting Skills:</ansi>
  <ansi fg="stat">blacksmithing</ansi> — Metal weapons, armor, tools
  <ansi fg="stat">alchemy</ansi>       — Potions, salves, medicines
  <ansi fg="stat">tailoring</ansi>     — Cloth and leather goods
  <ansi fg="stat">cooking</ansi>       — Food preparation, buffs
  <ansi fg="stat">jewelcrafting</ansi> — Rings, pendants, gemwork
  <ansi fg="stat">enchanting</ansi>    — Imbuing items with magic

All skills progress through use. See <ansi fg="command">help rhetoric</ansi>
for the new conviction combat skill.
